Heapify operation - O(n) Time and O(n) SpaceHeapify is an operation that places a node in its correct position in a heap so that the subtree rooted at that node satisfies the heap property.To build a max heap from an unsorted array, we start from the last non-leaf node and move up to the root, calling heapify on each node. For each node, if it is smaller than any of its children, we swap it with the largest child and continue until it is larger than both children. After all nodes are processed, the array becomes a valid max heap. 
